  "query_preview": "..The sky was clear to partly cloudy across most of\nsoutheast Arizona this morning. The exception was increasing\nclouds across western Pima county associated with upper low off\nnorthern Baja. Radar was showing widely scattered showers moving\ninto Yuma county and western Pima county. For today scattered\nlight showers will be around. Scattered showers will be around\nagain on Monday with a few storms developing during daytime\nheating. A system moving out of the Gulf of Alaska this morning\nwill move down the west coast this week, keeping daily chances\nof showers across SE Arizona for the rest of the work week.\n\nTemperatures through the forecast period will generally be slightly \nbelow normal, though near normal temperatures will occur around \nTuesday and Wednesday.",
